// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 3 „Minevik ja kogemused” (b1b2-011…015), stage B1+.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, one year after the B1 course: Sofia is a
// project manager at Tuul Logistika — a work trip to Riga that went wrong and the successful move of the Tartu city
// library; Markus records Viktor's memories of the 1990s for the city museum. The goal, said on the first sheet: at the
// end the learner writes a structured incident report and gives an oral retrospective at a team meeting (014 Kasuta).
// Grammar: the three past tenses tied to their function (grammarPlan „pasts”: 011 lihtminevik = an event, 012 täisminevik
// = an experience, 013 enneminevik = what had happened before), deepened for B2: tense choice in a narrative (011, 014),
// the past conditional oleksin teinud (taught in 012, used again in 014), the impersonal past tehti / oli tehtud (taught
// in 013, used again in 014). Module 2's words (linnavalitsus, taotlus, luba, e-teenus, üürima, remont, arve, rike,
// asendusbuss, tühistama, kaebus…) come back in the trip, the permit and the claim.
//   011 Sofia's voice message from a broken-down bus, her e-mail about the night in Riga; Markus's version for the
//       firm's paper, what went wrong and how it was solved; the bus company's rules — a call and a claim for refund.
//   012 the firm's paper introduces the library project team, Anna's mountain story; an interview with Kertu, Artur's
//       cover letter, „what would you have done differently?”; the candidates' cards, the interview, the choice, a letter.
//   013 Sofia and Liis rebuild the moving day (a wrong date in the permit), the town paper's news; Sofia's call to Merle
//       Kuusk at the town government, Merle's summary; the meeting with Merle and a written explanation.
//   014 Markus interviews Viktor about 1993 for the museum, Markus's story of the night at the farm; Sofia's project
//       retrospective, Viktor's museum card; the final project — Liis's message, an oral retrospective, an incident report.
// Harno B2 formats trained: a 4-option gap text (012), a sentence-bank text (013), a semi-formal letter of ~140 words
